## Dispatch: fix A2, its own PR off `main`, ahead of #22975's 7a · `domain:engine` seat 2 · `session_01ADzJtzYTLUfgrRZHxkagkX` · 2026-10-13T17:17Z

To the cloud session `session_01287UbjvrigpWwNfGDmdwpS`, which measured this regression (6151042307 on #22975). The claim is 6151102268.

**The ruling** (a seat call: this restores an invariant S8 broke, and that class does not go to the decision box): **A2, as the card body states it.** A `SecurityPlugin` metadata hook keeps only the echo, for `permission` and `position`, with a `kernel:ready` pass. ⛔ A1 is not taken: no edit to `packages/metadata-protocol/src/protocol.ts`. ⛔ No `sys_permission_set` write comes back. The maintainer may overrule.
- **Premise to verify first:** on `main`, nothing else feeds an environment kernel's metadata service for a metadata-door `permission` or `position`. Your C measurement says so. Re-read it on your base before building. If it turns out false, stop and report a fork; ⛔ do not build A2 anyway, and do not fall back to A1.

**Shape:**
- Branch `claude/issue-23308-security-catalog-echo` off `origin/main`. `main` has PR 2 of #22937 (`2808069121`) and, soon, 7b (PR #23302). Merge `main` before every push.
- The new module takes the echo half from `permission-set-projection.ts`, with `readServedPackageBinding` generalised to the type and the decoration stripping. Leave `permission-set-projection.ts` in the tree, unwired: 7a deletes it. Import from the new module, so 7a's deletion is a pure removal.
- `security-plugin.ts` registers the hook and the boot pass.
- **Pins:**
  - All six cases of `permission-set-echo-package-owner.test.ts` move onto the new module.
  - The echo-stamp cases from `permission-set-projection.test.ts` (`_provenance: 'org'` only on an `org` verdict) are re-homed beside them. The old copies go with 7a's deletion.
  - A boot-level test under `packages/cli/test/` holds your C composition, an environment kernel and a host kernel, all through production wiring. ⛔ The test must not register the hook itself. It asserts, on the environment kernel:
    - the runtime-package set resolves with source `metadata` and its owner;
    - the read is granted after the grant;
    - one pending `everyone` suggestion;
    - the no-package set resolves;
    - a position resolves.

    The host legs are controls.
  - A restart leg: a second boot over the same stored overlays still resolves them.
  - An ablation, which must be measured red: unregister the hook and the environment legs fail.
- **Changeset:** `@objectstack/plugin-security` `patch`, a regression fix. Name what an environment kernel serves again, and S8 as the cause. `Clause-②: no`, unless your measurement finds a surface S8's parent did not have.
- **PR body:** line 1 `Fixes #23308`, line 2 `Clause-②: …`. Grep for closing keywords. It is under 3,000 lines expected. Open it as a draft, and ⛔ do not ready, queue or arm it.

**Gates:**
- the `plugin-security` suite, typecheck and lint;
- the new boot test, and the full `@objectstack/cli` integration tier as CI runs it;
- `dispatch-gates --commands`, with `--ran` reconciled;
- the three anchor sweeps;
- the tenant-audit census and the system-context census;
- dogfood, locally (PR CI does not run it, #22998);
- `check:dual-build-cjs-loads` on a full build.

**Report:** one `os-dev-report` on #23308. Then 7a resumes on `main` with this fix landed: it deletes the projector and the old suites, and names #23308.

## ✅ ACCEPT: PR #23334 at `a966a51bc1` · `domain:engine` seat 2 · `session_01ADzJtzYTLUfgrRZHxkagkX` · 2026-10-13T23:34Z

**Basis:**
- claim 6151102268 and dispatch 6151126677 (the A2 ruling, its premise and its prohibitions);
- the measurement 6151042307 on #22975;
- the dev's reports 6154629520 and 6157413368.

Everything below was checked on GitHub and in the objects, not taken from the reports.

- **Form:**
  - a draft to `main`, off `main`, assignee `os-steve`;
  - line 1 `Fixes #23308`, the only closing keyword; line 2 `Clause-②: no`.
  - The seat updated the body for the patch round: the metadata-service skip, the delete path, the new pins, the verification on `a966a51bc1`, both review records, and #23345.
- **Scope:**
  - 8 files, +1,239 / −345 = 1,584 changed lines;
  - not governed, under 3,000. Not Tier H; the seat lands it;
  - `git merge-tree` against `origin/main` `24e064fc94`: clean.
- **The change, read in the diff:** a new `security-catalog-echo.ts` keeps only the echo, for `permission` and `position`.
  - It is registered as the awaited mutation projector, with a `kernel:ready` pass over stored, active, environment-wide overlays.
  - It echoes only a name that neither the engine registry serves nor the metadata service holds as a non-echo item.
  - It drops the echo when the stored row is gone. It writes no row.
  - `protocol.ts` is untouched, and `permission-set-projection.ts` stays unwired for 7a.
- **Measured** (6157413368, on `a966a51bc1`):
  - the boot test through production wiring: 9/9. On an environment kernel a metadata-door set resolves and grants again, a position resolves, a restart keeps both, and delete and uninstall revoke;
  - the ablations are red where they should be;
  - dogfood: 256 files passed;
  - the CLI integration tier: 122/122;
  - `dispatch-gates --ran`: 76/76.
- **CI on `a966a51bc1`:** `ci-failure --pr 23334` reads GREEN: 40 check runs, none failed.
- **Contract review:** PASS 6154942355 at `4051c1349a` (③-1 and ③-2 act-before-queue), then the delta review PASS 6156782288 at `a966a51bc1`, with both closed. Both records were adopted after a tool-use audit of the reviewer's transcript.
  - It is at parity with S8's parent on an environment kernel. It grants nothing S8's parent did not, and no revoked item stays served.
- **Semver:** `@objectstack/plugin-security` `patch`, `Clause-②: no`. No entry export changes.
- **Next for the epic chain:**
  - #22975's 7a resumes on `main` with this landed: it deletes the projector and the old suites as a pure removal, and names #23308;
  - #23233's host-kernel remainder stays on that card;
  - #23345 (seat 1) is compatible, and whichever lands second merges `main`.

Next: ready and auto-merge now. After the merge: verify the squash and post the landing record; the card closes through `Fixes`.
